{
  "sn12.60:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.60 ",
  "sn12.60:0.2": "6. Suffering ",
  "sn12.60:0.3": "Causation ",
  "sn12.60:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Kurus, near the Kuru town named Kammāsadamma. ",
  "sn12.60:1.2": "Then Venerable Ānanda went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "sn12.60:1.3": "“It’s incredible, sir! It’s amazing, ",
  "sn12.60:1.4": "in that this dependent origination is deep and appears deep, yet to me it seems as plain as can be.” ",
  "sn12.60:2.1": "“Not so, Ānanda! Not so, Ānanda! ",
  "sn12.60:2.2": "This dependent origination is deep and appears deep. ",
  "sn12.60:2.3": "It is because of not understanding and not penetrating this teaching that this population has become tangled like string, knotted like a ball of thread, and matted like rushes and reeds, and it doesn’t escape the places of loss, the bad places, the underworld, transmigration. ",
  "sn12.60:3.1": "There are things that fuel grasping. When you concentrate on the gratification provided by these things, your craving grows. ",
  "sn12.60:3.2": "Craving is a requirement for grasping. ",
  "sn12.60:3.3": "Grasping is a requirement for continued existence. ",
  "sn12.60:3.4": "Continued existence is a requirement for rebirth. ",
  "sn12.60:3.5": "Rebirth is a requirement for old age and death, sorrow, lamentation, pain, sadness, and distress to come to be. ",
  "sn12.60:3.6": "That is how this entire mass of suffering originates. ",
  "sn12.60:4